' ---------- Notes ----------
note right of Money
  All amounts use exact decimal values.
  Money is used as an attribute type across modules;
  the arrows are omitted to keep the diagram readable.
end note

note bottom of Wallet
  No stored balance field.
  Available and held balances are computed
  from the sum of ledger entries per bucket.
  Every financial operation has a unique FinancialMovement
  idempotency key and may append multiple ledger entries.
  A hold writes AVAILABLE negative and HELD positive postings.
  Check and reserve against the ledger-derived available total
  atomically; competing holds cannot reserve the same funds.
end note

note bottom of Account
  Registration fields are not defined in the brief (AQ-01).
  Agent authentication is not defined (AQ-04).
  Role SYSTEM is PayLink's own fee-income account.
end note

note bottom of PaymentState
  State pattern. Only the transitions of the brief are allowed.
  Any other event is rejected with an invalid-transition error.
  Every transition adds a PaymentStatusHistory row. Failed ->
  Refunded occurs with successful hold release. Completed, Rejected
  and Refunded are terminal; FR-27 does not add Completed -> Refunded.
end note

note bottom of RefundRequest
  Refund of a Completed payment (FR-27).
  Separate from the Failed to Refunded hold release,
  which is a Failed -> Refunded transition plus a RELEASE movement.
  On 2026-11-25 the user approved deferring FR-27 implementation
  and method/amount/ledger definition until team/TA resolves AQ-07/AQ-12.
  The user separately approved one authorized Support-role reviewer
  and an audit record of actor, timestamp, outcome, reason, payment/refund
  identifiers and any resulting ledger movement; no dual control is proposed.
  Team/TA confirmation is pending; neither is team/TA approval. No
  completed-refund method or state transition is approved.
end note

note bottom of InquireBillerStatusCommand
  Command pattern. Re-queries the biller after
  User-approved AQ-15 offsets (2026-11-25): 1, 5 and 15 minutes
  from Unknown entry. Rationale: deterministic times from the start of
  the unresolved state. This is user approval, not team/TA approval.
  It never re-sends the payment.
end note

note bottom of FraudRuleHandler
  Chain of Responsibility.
  Order: AccountStatus, SingleLimit, DailyLimit, Velocity.
  Limits and windows are read from ConfigurationService.
  User-approved AQ-14 interpretation (2026-11-25): count payment initiation
  attempts including those later rejected. This is user approval, not a claim
  of team/TA approval. Rationale: prevent rapid activity evading the rule
  through rejected outcomes. Daily limit composition remains open.
  The caller builds FraudCheckContext and applies blockAccountUntil.
end note

note bottom of ElectroCoAdapter
  Phase 2 API v2 change (field mapping, piaster conversion,
  request signing) is confined to this adapter.
end note

note right of BillerService
  Catalog fields include biller-specific inputs such as
  ElectroCo meter number and TopUpNet phone number.
end note

note bottom of BillerAdapterFactory
  Factory selects by biller code from the configured adapter registry.
  Adding a biller means one new adapter plus registry/configuration;
  unrelated modules and the payment workflow do not change.
end note

note bottom of TopUpNetAdapter
  `accepted` is a pending integration result, not a payment state.
  Payment stays SentToBiller until a definitive callback; callback
  state changes are validated by PaymentState.
end note

note bottom of ConfigurationItem
  Business rules live here, not in code:
  daily limits, 5 and 10,000 payment range, fees,
  40 percent commission, velocity rule, timeouts, retries.
end note

@enduml
